== Usage ==

Place this infobox at the start of an item page. All fields are optional.
Blank fields hide their rows and mean unknown, not zero.

<pre>
{{Item
| icon =
| category =
| level =
| optimal =
| classes =
| restrictions =
| damage =
| delay =
| attacktype =
| defense =
| magicdefense =
| attributes =
| hq =
| recast =
| duration =
| effect =
| repair =
| material =
| baseitem =
| dyes =
| materia =
| melds =
| catalyst =
| stack =
| flags =
| price =
| patch =
}}
</pre>

<code>icon</code> is the item's client icon ID. It selects the uploaded image
<code>File:XIVL_&lt;id&gt;.png</code>. <code>hq</code> describes the bonus from
the high-quality version, including the attribute and amount, such as
"Strength +5".

Use <code>level</code> for a required level. Use <code>optimal</code> for gear
that can be equipped at any level but reduces its stats to match the wearer's
level. It provides its full stats only at the optimal level. An item uses one of
these fields, never both.

Enter only numbers for <code>delay</code>, <code>recast</code>, and
<code>duration</code>. The template adds their units.

For materia, <code>effect</code> describes the melded effect,
<code>melds</code> lists compatible equipment slots, and <code>catalyst</code>
names the catalyst it converts from. For gear, <code>materia</code> records
whether the item can be melded and converted.
</noinclude>
